<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The quarrel gene (built 2026-09-30, CASTES-PLAN.md phase 1). One mechanism,
		two castes, two dials: the soldier beetle turns it on her own kind, so the
		dislike is mutual, and the hornet turns it on the honey bees, so it is one
		way. Both decided 2026-09-30.

		The dial is `QuarrelGeneExtension.dislikedGene` - the gene whose carriers she
		cannot stand. Source/Insects/Quarrel.cs answers vanilla's social-thought
		question with it, and the -50 lives on the two thought defs
		(Defs/ThoughtDefs/Thoughts_NewCastes.xml).

		The fights need no code of their own, and that is the useful part:
		`Pawn_InteractionsTracker` already scales the social-fight chance by opinion
		(x2.5 at -50, x4 at -100), so "much more likely to start a fight with them"
		comes out of the opinion penalty by itself, pairwise, from the engine.

		The two defs differ in nothing but that one line, which is the point: a third
		grudge is a third def and no new code.

		Displayed lines: none, on purpose. Neither def carries a stat offset, so
		their effect boxes stay empty and the description below is what the player
		reads. The opinion shows up where opinions belong - in the social tab, as
		"quarrelsome kin" or "smell of honey".
	-->
	<GeneDef>
		<defName>PMM_Gene_Quarrelsome</defName>
		<label>quarrelsome</label>
		<description>Her own kind sets her teeth on edge. Another woman carrying this same temper is someone she cannot stand the sight of, and the feeling runs both ways - which is what a village of soldier beetles is like.</description>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_Quarrelsome</iconPath>
		<geneClass>PMM_Insects.Gene_Quarrel</geneClass>
		<displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
		<displayOrderInCategory>1003</displayOrderInCategory>
		<!-- A drawback pays a little back, the vanilla convention (Sleepy and Sterile both
		     give a point). -50 opinion toward her own kind is worth one. -->
		<biostatMet>1</biostatMet>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.QuarrelGeneExtension">
				<!-- Aimed at itself: every carrier dislikes every other carrier. -->
				<dislikedGene>PMM_Gene_Quarrelsome</dislikedGene>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</GeneDef>

	<GeneDef>
		<defName>PMM_Gene_HoneyHatred</defName>
		<label>honey-hating</label>
		<description>Hornets and bees were never friends, and the smell of honey is an insult. A woman carrying the honey gene is someone she cannot stand - though the honey bee herself feels nothing of the sort.</description>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_HoneyHatred</iconPath>
		<geneClass>PMM_Insects.Gene_Quarrel</geneClass>
		<displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
		<displayOrderInCategory>1004</displayOrderInCategory>
		<!-- Same reasoning as the quarrel above: one point back for a one-way grudge. -->
		<biostatMet>1</biostatMet>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.QuarrelGeneExtension">
				<!-- Aimed at the honey gene, and only that way round: the bee never notices. -->
				<dislikedGene>PMM_Gene_Honey</dislikedGene>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</GeneDef>

</Defs>
